        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-22",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Multipart filename sanitized before HTML-unescape, allowing path separators to be reintroduced.\n\nThe uploaded filename from the attacker-controlled Content-Disposition header is passed through os.path.basename() (line 215) BEFORE html.unescape() (line 217); html.unescape can reintroduce '/' (e.g. '&#47;') and path components after basename has already run, so the value handed to upload handlers can contain traversal sequences.\n\nImpact: The parser emits file names such as '../../../x' or '..' from crafted/HTML-encoded Content-Disposition filenames. This is the weakness class behind CVE-2021-31542 (this snapshot dated 2021-04-06 predates the May 2021 fix that reordered sanitization and added validate_file_name). Whether traversal reaches the filesystem depends on downstream consumers; django/core/files/uploadedfile.py re-applies os.path.basename (neutralizing embedded '/'), but a name of exactly '..' still passes through both basename calls and can cause directory traversal when the application saves the file under uploaded_file.name via Storage.\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker submits multipart/form-data with Content-Disposition filename='..' (or an HTML-encoded separator sequence). The parser produces file_name='..', which survives UploadedFile._set_name's basename. An application that saves the upload using the provided name (a common pattern) then writes/overwrites a path one directory above the intended upload location.\n\nPreconditions: Application saves uploaded files using the client-supplied name (uploaded_file.name) via a Storage backend; Downstream Storage does not independently reject '..'/path components (out of scope for django/http).\n\nRecommendation: Apply html.unescape and force_str before os.path.basename, and explicitly reject names that are '.', '..', or contain path separators (as done by the later validate_file_name fix).\n\nCWE-22. Severity MEDIUM, confidence low."
          },
          "locations": [
